From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: SetPixelFormat on a pbuffer's DC.

Java 3D (Sweet Home 3D's 3D view) takes a pbuffer's DC with wglGetPbufferDCARB,
sets the pbuffer's own pixel format on it and makes its offscreen context there.
set_pixel_format refused every DC that is not a window's ("not a valid window DC"):
Java 3D reported "Failed in SetPixelFormat" and Sweet Home 3D closed with a fatal
error in its 3D rendering system. A pbuffer's DC already has the pbuffer's format;
as on a window whose format is set, setting that format again succeeds and any
other fails. (On Mesa's software rasterizer Java 3D then meets a GLX pbuffer
limit of drisw; on a GPU's GL the 3D view works.)
---
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
index c806431..104b62a 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
@@ -1287,6 +1287,25 @@ static BOOL set_pixel_format( HDC hdc, int format, BOOL internal )
 
     if (!hwnd || hwnd == NtUserGetDesktopWindow())
     {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PBUFFER_DC_NO_FORMAT
+        struct gl_drawable *gl;
+
+        /* A pbuffer's DC already has the pbuffer's format, which setting
+         * again succeeds, as on a window whose format is set; any other
+         * fails. Java 3D (Sweet Home 3D) sets it on the DC it gets from
+         * wglGetPbufferDCARB before making its offscreen context. */
+        if (!hwnd && (gl = get_gl_drawable( NULL, hdc )))
+        {
+            int current = pixel_format_index( gl->format );
+            BOOL ret;
+
+            if (!is_onscreen_pixel_format( current )) current = 1;
+            ret = gl->type == DC_GL_PBUFFER && current == format;
+            TRACE( "pbuffer DC %p format %d, asked %d -> %d\n", hdc, current, format, ret );
+            release_gl_drawable( gl );
+            return ret;
+        }
+#endif
         WARN( "not a valid window DC %p/%p\n", hdc, hwnd );
         return FALSE;
     }
